/* book exam traps: Δf is half the tone spacing: for 30 kHz and 20 kHz tones Δf = 5 kHz, not 10 kHz, and h = 1. | Orthogonality needs a whole multiple: nRb/2 for coherent and nRb for non-coherent detection. 7.5 kHz at 10 kb/s is above the minimum and still not orthogonal. | In B = 2(Δf + Rb), Rb is the bit rate in bit/s; putting in Tb gives nonsense. | For OOK, Eb is the average A²Tb/4. Using the burst energy A²Tb/2 makes OOK look 3 dB better than it is. | Coherent detection needs a phase-locked carrier; an envelope detector is non-coherent and has other formulas. */
