/* book exam traps: BPSK is Q(√(2Eb/N0)); Q(√(Eb/N0)) is coherent BFSK or OOK. Dropping the 2 costs 3 dB. | Q(x) and erfc differ by a factor and a √2: Q(x) = ½erfc(x/√2), so Pb = ½erfc(√(Eb/N0)). Mixing the two forms is the commonest numeric slip. | The null-to-null bandwidth of rectangular BPSK is 2Rb, not Rb. | A carrier phase error θ scales the amplitude by cos θ and the energy by cos²θ; at 90° BPSK fails completely. | The correlator output is in √J, not volts; the noise on it has variance N0/2, not N0. */
