/* book: lead: A coherent receiver needs a local carrier locked to the phase of the incoming one. When the oscillators drift, or the receiver must be cheap, non-coherent detection does without that phase. For FSK and OOK it measures envelopes; for phase keying it puts the data in the change of phase from one bit to the next, which is differential phase shift keying (DPSK). The price is a small loss in error prob */
